HNS i2h Banner/New-Tab Development
Context:
Working on timax.al-githubio website with existing i2h (ICANN to Handshake) redirect scripts in i2h that currently do direct pass-through redirects.

Requirement:
Instead of redirecting users away from the ICANN site, display a banner that opens the HNS version in a NEW TAB, keeping the original page accessible (since HNS sites won't have return navigation).

Current Setup:

Existing scripts: handshake.js, redirect.js, https.js (all do location.href redirects)
No pages currently implement HNS pass-through
Site uses modern theming with light/dark/black modes
Confirmed HNS Mirrors:

aboutlife.html → http://aboutlife/ (confirmed working with Fingertip)
Potentially others to be identified
Proposed Solution:
Create site-helpers/i2h/handshake-newtab.js that:

Detects Handshake-capable browsers
Shows dismissible banner at top of page
Provides link to open HNS version in new tab (target="_blank")
Adapts to site's theme system
Non-intrusive, preserves ICANN page functionality
Implementation:
Add to page <head>: <script src="../../site-helpers/i2h/handshake-newtab.js" domain="aboutlife" protocol="http"></script>

Tasks:

Create the handshake-newtab.js script
Test with aboutlife.html as proof-of-concept
Apply to other pages with HNS mirrors


potential new script offered by copilot:
``` 
(function() {
  const targetDomain = document.currentScript.getAttribute('domain');
  const targetProtocol = document.currentScript.getAttribute('protocol') || 'https';
  
  // Check if browser can resolve Handshake (simple detection)
  if (location.hostname !== targetDomain) {
    // Create a button/link to open HNS version in new tab
    const hnsUrl = `${targetProtocol}://${targetDomain}${location.pathname}`;
    
    // Add a banner at top of page
    const banner = document.createElement('div');
    banner.style.cssText = 'position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; background: rgba(52, 4, 244, 0.9); color: white; padding: 10px; text-align: center; z-index: 10000; font-family: Arial;';
    banner.innerHTML = `<span>🌐 Handshake-enabled browser detected! </span><a href="${hnsUrl}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #ccffff; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline; margin-left: 10px;">Open HNS version ↗</a><button onclick="this.parentElement.remove()" style="float: right; background: transparent; border: 1px solid white; color: white; cursor: pointer; border-radius: 3px; padding: 2px 8px;">✕</button>`;
    
    document.body.insertAdjacentElement('afterbegin', banner);
  }
})();
```

and Implementation for aboutlife.html
Add to the <head> section:
```
<!-- HNS Redirect - Opens in new tab for Handshake-capable browsers -->
<script src="../../site-helpers/i2h/handshake-newtab.js" domain="aboutlife" protocol="http"></script>
```

